query:
ClickHouse Keeper disconnects after addWatch() (breaks CuratorCache startup)

### Describe what's wrong

Hi!

I noticed a recent PR where AddWatch was added, and I decided to check how it would work in our application, which currently uses ZooKeeper:
https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/88813

We use Apache Curator, specifically CuratorCache. I know Curator also has a create2 operation that isn’t supported, but the problem is different: when the cache starts, the logs show a lot of “connection lost” and “reconnected” messages, and the cache never actually finishes starting.

It turned out that CuratorCache calls addWatch during startup. After that, a reconnect happens, addWatch is triggered again, and it loops infinitely.

I tried to write a simple Java test that calls addWatch, and after that the client gets disconnected. This does not happen when using ZooKeeper instead of ClickHouse Keeper. It looks like if we can figure out why a disconnect happens after calling addWatch, it will also fix the CuratorCache startup issue.

Could you please advise whether I’m doing something wrong on my side, or whether there might be an issue in ClickHouse Keeper?

### Does it reproduce on the most recent release?

Yes

### How to reproduce

ClickHouse Keeper: 26.1.3.52
ZooKeeper library: 3.7.1
Apache Curator: 5.4.0
```xml
<clickhouse>
    <keeper_server>
        <tcp_port>2181</tcp_port>
        <server_id>1</server_id>
        <log_storage_path>./keeper-logs</log_storage_path>
        <snapshot_storage_path>./keeper-snapshots</snapshot_storage_path>
        <raft_configuration>
            <server>
                <id>1</id>
                <hostname>localhost</hostname>
                <port>9444</port>
            </server>
        </raft_configuration>
    </keeper_server>
</clickhouse>
```
